>The problem is, I can't find any stairs leading down on level 30, and I
>have looked *EVERYWHERE*.  Help!  I have a wand of digging ... can I
>make this dig downwards?  

A couple of facts:
     Don't even bother to look for stairways going down from there -
       there aren't any.
     Teleporting while confused will level teleport you.
     Reading cursed scrolls or teleportation or using a level teleporter
       will have the same effect.

>Also, since I have been down in the mazes and
>crowned the Hand of Elbereth, every time I pray to Lugh, I am told
>he is angry with me ... what the hell have I done to get him pissed?

This doesn't have anything to do with the fact that you're in the mazes.  The
plain and simple problem is that you've been crowned the Hand of Elbereth.
You have a "prayer time-out" period (which is random), which determines
how long you have to wait before praying again in order to avoid pissing 
your god off.  For starting characters, this is usually about 300 turns, so
a good rule is to wait a minimum of 300 turns in between prayers.  For the
Hand, on the other hand (no pun intended :-), this is about 3000 turns, so
basically once you've been crowned the Hand of Elbereth you're expected to
do things on your own, and only pray to your god once in a LONG, LONG while.

